[02:57.95] Overhead the albatross
[03:01.34] Hangs motionless upon the air
[03:05.43] And deep beneath the rolling waves
[03:09.37] In labyrinths of coral caves
[03:13.38] The echo of a distant time
[03:16.30] Comes willowing across the sand
[03:20.55] And everything is green and submarine
[03:28.00] And no one showed us to the land
[03:32.38] And no one knows the wheres or whys
[03:35.86] But something stirs and something tries
[03:39.38] And starts to climb towards the light
[03:47.46] 
[04:12.07] Strangers passing in the street
[04:15.63] By chance two separate glances meet
[04:19.21] And I am you and what I see is me
[04:26.44] And do I take you by the hand?
[04:30.60] And lead you through the land?
[04:33.93] And help me understand the best I can?
[04:41.33] And no one calls us to move on
[04:44.94] And no one forces down our eyes
[04:48.65] And no one speaks and no one tries
[04:51.91] And no one flies around the sun
[04:59.80] 
[19:11.86] Cloudless everyday you fall
[19:15.79] Upon my waking eyes
[19:19.26] Inviting and inciting me to rise
[19:27.20] And through the window in the wall
[19:30.58] Come streaming in on sunlight wings
[19:34.36] A million bright ambassadors of morning
[19:41.68] And no one sings me lullabies
[19:45.34] And no one makes me close my eyes
[19:49.32] And so I throw the windows wide
[19:52.32] Callin' you across the sky
[19:58.28] 